 favorable to him than Republican-sponsored surveys. Expert forecasters mostly call the race Lean Democratic, though several rate it a Tossup, and prediction markets put Democratic win odds near 70 percent. The race remains genuinely competitive, with turnout and the national environment likely to decide the outcome.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7769, "margin": 3.59}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7646, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7534, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7553, "margin": 3.4}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6955, "margin": 3.2}]}